  ▐ aura  Working tree is clean — so the bug isn't a working-tree edit; it's simply this old commit (Django 2.2-era, mid-2019) predating the upstream fix for this exact issue (ticket #24205). The cause is in `construct_instance` (django/forms/models.py:51-53): when a model field has a default and its widget's value was omitted from the POST data, the field is skipped entirely — so even a non-empty `cleaned_data` (e.g. injected in `form.clean()`) can't override the default. The upstream fix adds a check that `cleaned_data` is actually empty before leaving the default in place.

