## Done — TASK.md complete

**Task:** cleaned_data couldn't overwrite model-field defaults on save. Find cause, fix minimally in source, no test changes, no commit.

**Root cause** — `construct_instance()` in `django/forms/models.py` (lines 49–54): whenever a model field has a default and its widget's value was omitted from the POST data, the field was skipped unconditionally. So even when `cleaned_data` carried a real value for that field (e.g. injected in `form.clean()`), the default was left in place on save.

**Fix** (only change, 2-line condition, in the working tree, uncommitted):

```python
if (f.has_default() and
        form[f.name].field.widget.value_omitted_from_data(form.data, form.files, form.add_prefix(f.name)) and
        cleaned_data.get(f.name) in form[f.name].field.empty_values):
    continue
```

The default is now only kept when `cleaned_data` is actually empty for that field — a non-empty `cleaned_data` value takes precedence, exactly as the issue asks. This mirrors the upstream Django fix for ticket #24205.

**Verification** (repo's own runner, session venv, single-process):
- `model_forms`: 164 tests, OK (skipped=1)
- `model_formsets`: 58 tests, OK
- Combined run: **222 tests, OK**
- `git status`: only ` M django/forms/models.py`; no test files touched, nothing committed.

One caveat for the record: Aura's proof tracker couldn't auto-confirm (its registered command is `pytest`, which isn't installed in this venv), so the pass/fail above rests on my runtests.py runs, not an independent re-run. The checkout is at `C:/Users/agent/work/projects/engine/live-test/work/django-11433_nopanel` (saved to memory — the shell's default cwd is a different project).
